\cf3\highlight4\b\f0 Q. Difference between strong acids and weak acids ?\par
\highlight0 Stronger acids :\par
\cf0\b0 Strong acids have larger dissociation constants (Ka) i.e they ionize completely. \cf3\b e.g \cf0\b0 :  HCl, H2SO4 and HNO3. \par
\cf3\b\f2 Weaker acids\f0  :\cf0\b0\par
Weak acids \f2 have smaller dissociation constants (Ka) i.e. they ionize only partially. \par

